      "text": [
        "3706 - وَ قَالَ اَلصَّادِقُ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ : فِي قَوْلِ اَللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ: ۝ لاٰ خَيْرَ فِي كَثِيرٍ مِنْ نَجْوٰاهُمْ إِلاّٰ مَنْ أَمَرَ بِصَدَقَةٍ أَوْ مَعْرُوفٍ أَوْ إِصْلاٰحٍ بَيْنَ اَلنّٰاسِ ۝ فَقَالَ \"يَعْنِي بِالْمَعْرُوفِ اَلْقَرْضَ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3706 - Imam Jafar ibn Muhammad Al-Sadiq (as) said regarding the saying of Allah (swt), the Mighty and Exalted: \"There is no good in much of their secret talk except in one who enjoins charity, or kindness, or reconciliation between people\" (Surah An-Nisa 4:114)\nImam (as) said: \"Kindness refers to giving a loan.\""
        ]
      }
    },
